# Template for secrets.yaml (gitignored) in this same directory.
# scripts/write-secrets.sh (the `write-secrets` nx target, run before every
# build) generates secrets.yaml from it, taking each key from
# MEDIA_ROOM_DASHBOARD_<UPPERCASED_KEY> in the environment or in
# apps/media-room-dashboard/.env. A hand-written secrets.yaml is never
# overwritten. See README.md "Secrets".
#
# No station wifi credentials here on purpose — the device gets those via
# its (open, unpassworded) captive-portal setup flow at first boot instead
# (see README.md).

# Native API encryption key (32 bytes, base64). Generate your own with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Enter this same value in HA when it prompts for the encryption key while
# adding the discovered device under Settings > Devices & Services.
# The real key is this remote's own (never shared with other apps):
# MEDIA_ROOM_DASHBOARD_API_ENCRYPTION_KEY, kept in bws as
# media-room-dashboard/MEDIA_ROOM_DASHBOARD_API_ENCRYPTION_KEY and as the
# same-named GitHub Actions secret for release builds.
# The placeholder below is a validly-formatted but not-secret example key —
# it only needs to satisfy ESPHome's format validation for placeholder
# builds (PR/CI validation), replace it with your own generated key.
api_encryption_key: "f0aQMe3RzMHKjV0COPgwXknBICzGef6+ejORSu9VVpM="
